<title>MEXICO: Mexico lists hectares planted by grain in 97 crop.</title>
<headline>Mexico lists hectares planted by grain in 97 crop.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agriculture Ministry estimated hectares of grain planted for the 1997 spring-summer harvest cycle, in a recent report obtained by Reuters.</p>
<p>The following are the ministry's estimates and comparative figures from the year-ago period.</p>
<p>		   1997 Spring-Summer*	    1996 Spring-Summer</p>
<p>    Rice	     1,400 hectares		  1,600 hectares</p>
<p>    Bean	    63,200 hectares		 29,700 hectares</p>
<p>    Corn	   946,800 hectares		561,100 hectares</p>
<p>    Wheat	    2,000 hectares		  3,200 hectares</p>
<p>    Cotton	  98,400 hectares		166,700 hectares</p>
<p>    Soy Bean	   200 hectares			0 hectares</p>
<p>    Barley	   1,000 hectares		  1,700 hectares</p>
<p>    Sorghum	 47,100 hectares		 74,800 hectares</p>
<p>  Total	  1.160 million hectares		838,800 hectares</p>
<p>*estimated figures through April 30</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
